  "label": "Satirical news broadcast",
  "description": "A genre of media that mimics the format and tone of serious news broadcasts but uses absurd, exaggerated, or offensive content for comedic or critical effect. The use of Ron Burgundy in a news studio setting is a classic example of this genre, which relies on the audience's familiarity with real news formats to enhance the humor or satire of the content.",
